{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["את אימתי — the terror of Elohim upon your adversaries." "והמתי — and I will cause panic (הִמָּתָה) by the confusion (מְהוּמָה) of My voice, as written: ״וירעם ה׳ בקול גדול על פלשתים ויהומם״. And similarly: ״ברק ויהום״. Like ״סבב סבותי״ — but the language of מיתה, he says, would be read וְהֵמַתִּי."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {1 "Rashbam argues the word is from the root המם (to confuse/panic), with the he of והמתי being a radical; the alternative reading וְהֵמַתִּי would derive from the root מות (to kill). The comparison to 'סבב סבותי' illustrates a similar morphological pattern of doubled/extended radicals."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:54.882378489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}